# Line-ending policy for this repository.
#
# Without this file, line endings are governed by each machine's local
# core.autocrlf setting, which is not versioned and does not travel with the
# repo. That produced a mixed working tree — some files CRLF, some LF — which
# makes byte-level comparison (hashing, diffing, byte-identity checks)
# unreliable, since identical content in the two conventions hashes
# differently.
#
# Pin it here instead: LF in the index and LF in the working tree, on every
# machine, regardless of local git config.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary formats. Git's text/binary auto-detection would classify these
# correctly today, but pinning them removes the dependency on that heuristic —
# a file wrongly treated as text gets its bytes rewritten and silently
# corrupted.

*.png   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.uf2   binary